# Apple MTP trackpads whose kernel driver decides palms by size itself.
#
# hid-magicmouse reports a palm as MT_TOOL_PALM from the controller's contact
# class on the T6041, J616s and K116s (Trackpad26) trackpads. On the T6041 it
# also marks a contact as a palm once its tool area alone passes palm size,
# which replaces libinput's Apple MTP palm size threshold (touch size 1600):
# a resting palm there has a touch size of about 1060, so that threshold never
# caught it. Turn it off where the kernel applies that size rule.
#
# Kept on elsewhere, for a hardware reason:
# - J616s and K116s: the kernel trusts the contact class only (J616s fingers
#   reach the tool area of the T6041 rule). J616s palms have a touch size of
#   1861-2358 and fingers stay under 230, so the threshold catches palms the
#   class misses and never a finger; the K116s has no recorded sizes yet.
# - Every other MTP trackpad: the kernel reports no palms, so the threshold
#   is its only palm detection. The J700 sends no touch size at all and has
#   its own quirk in aurora-neo-platform-config.
#
# libinput's quirks cannot match a udev property (MatchUdevType only takes
# the ID_INPUT_* types), and MatchDeviceTree sees only the first compatible,
# the board, so the T6041 boards with a trackpad are matched by name: the
# MacBook Pro 14-inch (J614c) and 16-inch (J616c).
[Apple MTP Touchpad, palms decided by size in the kernel]
MatchUdevType=touchpad
MatchName=Apple*MTP*
MatchVendor=0x05AC
MatchDeviceTree=apple,j61[46]c
AttrPalmSizeThreshold=0
